      <div type="clause" n="56">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 56</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="56" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="114" ed="#liebermann"/>C. Gif mon hwelcne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.22"/> ceap gebygð ⁊ he ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> onfinde him hwelc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.23"/> unhælo on<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.24"/> binnan XXX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.25"/> nihta, þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> weorpe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.26"/> þone ceap<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.27"/> to honda<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="***" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.star3"/>; oððe swerie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.28"/>, þæt he him nan facn on nyste, þa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.29"/> he hine him sealde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="56" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="114" ed="#liebermann"/>C. Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.9"/> hwylcne ceap gebygeþ<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.1"/> ⁊ he þonne onfinde him on hwylce unhælo binnon XXX nihta<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.12-2"/>, þonne weorpe he ðone ceap<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.2"/> to handa; oþþe swerige, þæt he him nan facen on nyste, þa he hine him sealde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="56" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="114" ed="#liebermann"/>Be gehwylces ceapes wyrðe. Gyf mon hwelcne ceap gebygeð ⁊ he ðonne afinde him hwylcne unhæle on binnon ðrittig nihta, ðonne weorpe ðone ceap to handa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.6"/>; oððe swerie, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he him nan facn on nyste, ða he hine him sealde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="56" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="115" ed="#liebermann"/>Si aliquod uiuum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.11"/> captale<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.star"/> persoluatur, et tunc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.12"/> inueniatur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.13"/> quelibet infirmitas in eo infra triginta noctes, reiciatur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.14"/> in manus to agenti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.15"/>; uel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.16"/> iuret, quod nullum facinus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.17"/> inesse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Ine_56.lnote.oe.18"/> sciebat, quando uendidit ei.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="54" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be gehwylces ceapes wyrðe.] Gif mon hwelcne ceap gebygð ⁊ he ðonne onfinde<ptr type="editorNote" n="19" target="#Ine_56.attnote.fn.19"/> him hwelce<ptr type="editorNote" n="20" target="#Ine_56.attnote.fn.20"/> unhælo<ptr type="editorNote" n="21" target="#Ine_56.attnote.fn.21"/> on binnan XXX nihta, þonne weorpe þone<ptr type="editorNote" n="22" target="#Ine_56.attnote.fn.22"/> ceap to honda<ptr type="editorNote" n="23" target="#Ine_56.attnote.fn.23"/>...oððe swerie, þæt he him nan facn on nyste, þa he hine him sealde.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="60" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="420" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{C} Gif mon hwelcne ceap gebygð ⁊ he ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> onfinde him hwelce unhælo on binnan XXX nihta, þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> weorpe þone ceap to honda; oððe swerie, þæt he him mnan facn on nyste, þa he hine him sealde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_56.lnote.de.1"/><pb n="115" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jemand irgend welches Vieh<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_56.lnote.de.2"/> kauft und er dann binnen 30 Nächten irgend welchen Krankheitsfehler an demselben findet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_56.lnote.de.3"/>, liefere er das Vieh (dem [früheren] Eigenthümer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_56.lnote.de.4"/>) aus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_56.lnote.de.5"/>; oder [dieser<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_56.lnote.de.6"/>] schwöre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_56.lnote.de.7"/>, dass er kein Fehl<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_56.lnote.de.8"/> daran kannte, als er es ihm verkaufte.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone buys any livestock and he then finds any defect of disease in it within 30 nights, let him hand the livestock back (to the [former] owner); or let [the latter] swear that he knew of no fault in it when he sold it to him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="55" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone buys any sort of beast, and then finds any manner of blemish in it within thirty days, he shall send it back to [its former] owner...or [the former owner]<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_56.attnote.n.1"/> shall swear that he knew of no blemish in it when he sold it him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="406" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone buys any cattle and he then finds any unsoundness in it within 30 days, he is to hand it back to the seller, or [the latter] is to swear that he knew of no fraud when he sold it to him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="421" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone buys any property and within thirty days he finds some flaw in it, then he should return the property to the hands [of the seller]; or [the seller] must swear that he knew of no defect when he sold it to him.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:Swer_7">Swer 7</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="421"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_77">Abt 77–81</ref> <quote>Compare to Hloþhere and Eadric §11 [L16]; see also Swerian §7 and §9. Æthelberht §76 [L77–81] similarly invokes the principle of unblemished goods</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="421"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Hl_16">Hl 16</ref> <quote>Compare to Hloþhere and Eadric §11 [L16]; see also Swerian §7 and §9. Æthelberht §76 [L77–81] similarly invokes the principle of unblemished goods</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="421"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Swer_7">Swer 7</ref> <quote>Compare to Hloþhere and Eadric §11 [L16]; see also Swerian §7 and §9. Æthelberht §76 [L77–81] similarly invokes the principle of unblemished goods</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="421"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Swer_9">Swer 9</ref> <quote>Compare to Hloþhere and Eadric §11 [L16]; see also Swerian §7 and §9. Æthelberht §76 [L77–81] similarly invokes the principle of unblemished goods</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_56.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> <hi rend="spaced">syllend</hi> <hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. eingefügt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> <hi rend="italic">syllend</hi> inserted in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_56.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">115</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">c. u. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">c. u. Lond</seg></note>
