        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_56.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rp <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rp So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_56.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ceape to handa <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ceape to handa Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_56.lnote.oe.star3" n="***" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðam syllende <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Ld, im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. B.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðam syllende added by Ld, in the 16th cent. B</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_56.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">swerige <hi rend="italic">Ld;</hi> spearige <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">swerige Ld; spearige So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_56.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þa þa hine se., <hi rend="italic">ohne</hi> he him <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þa þa hine se., without he him So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_56.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">78</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Rb stimmte nicht zum Inhalte; B ändert: ‘Vom Werte eines Stückes Vieh’, ohne zu bessern. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Handel 13</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The Rb did not fit the content; B alters it to ‘On the value of a head of cattle’, without improving it. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Handel 13</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_56.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">78</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Horn’s Zitat in Co zu Q bezieht sich wohl auf T; <hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> I S. <hi rend="smallcaps">xxii</hi> Z. 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Horn’s quotation in Co on Q probably refers to T; <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> I p. <hi rend="smallcaps">xxii</hi> l. 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_56.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">78</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">B modernisiert. — <hi rend="italic">him</hi> hängt von <hi rend="italic">on</hi> ab. — Ähnlich lautet Formel Swer 7; <hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> Einl. 11 a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">B modernises. — <hi rend="italic">him</hi> depends on <hi rend="italic">on</hi>. — The formula Swer 7 runs similarly; <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> Introduction 11 a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_56.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">78</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘dem Verkäufer’ Ld B, sinngemässe Zufügung (erst 16. Jhs.?). — In Q¹⁵ bessere <hi rend="italic">coagenti:</hi> ‘der Prozesspartei’; die Schreiber Q’s vermuteten wohl: <hi rend="italic">to agende</hi> Latinisiert</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘to the seller’ Ld B, an addition in keeping with the sense (not before the 16th cent.?). — In Q¹⁵ read <hi rend="italic">coagenti:</hi> ‘the party to the suit’; Q’s scribes probably took it for <hi rend="italic">to agende</hi> Latinised</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_56.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">78</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘zu Händen’ zu wörtlich; <hi rend="italic">weorpan to handa:</hi> ‘ausliefern’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘into the hands’ too literal; <hi rend="italic">weorpan to handa:</hi> ‘to hand over’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_56.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">78</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Archaisch fehlt Personale trotz Subjektswechsels</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Archaically, the personal pronoun is lacking despite the change of subject</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_56.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">78</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hier ist nur an Körperfehl gedacht, später bei diesem Anspruch auch an juristische Anfechtbarkeit des Eigentums: laut Swer 7. 9, wo dieselbe Eidesformel anklingt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Only a bodily defect is meant here; later this claim also covered legal challenges to the ownership: according to Swer 7. 9, where the same oath formula is echoed</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_56.lnote.de.8" n="8" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">78</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi> latinisierte nur <hi rend="italic">facn</hi> durch Endung; später ersetzt er es der Buchstabengleichheit wegen durch <hi rend="italic">facinus</hi> trotz anderen Sinnes</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi> Latinised <hi rend="italic">facn</hi> merely by an ending; later he replaces it with <hi rend="italic">facinus</hi> because of the similarity of letters, despite its different sense</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_56.attnote.fn.19" n="19" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><label>onfinde</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">afinde</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_56.attnote.fn.20" n="20" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><label>hwelce</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">on hwylce</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_56.attnote.fn.21" n="21" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><label>unhælo</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">hwylcne unhæle</hi>. B &amp; Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_56.attnote.fn.22" n="22" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><label>þone</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">he ðone</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_56.attnote.fn.23" n="23" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><label>honda</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">þam syllende</hi> added in B in 16th century.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_56.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">191</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The subject of <hi rend="italic">swerie</hi> must be the man who sold the beast; but the text can hardly be right as it stands. It would seem as if a number of words after <hi rend="italic">to honda</hi> had fallen out. For the form of the oath sworn by the buyer and seller of the cattle see <hi rend="italic">The Formulae for Oaths</hi>, cap. 7, 9.</seg></note>
      </div>
